### 13. `ih-post.md` — Indie Hackers post

**Voice:** Builder-to-builder. Messy, real numbers, honest failures. "I" not "we." Half-thoughts OK. Self-review gate: "Would I think AI wrote this?" If yes, rewrite messier.

**Title rules (hard):**
- ≤55 chars. Count before writing body. Rewrite if over.
- Must contain ≥1 digit (0-9). Spelled-out numbers don't count.
- No announcement framing. Ban openers: "Shipped", "Released", "Launched", "Just X", "Introducing", "Announcing", "New:", "v1.0/vN", "Update:". Outcomes or questions only.

**Body structure (hard):**
- First paragraph: lead with the takeaway, number, or outcome. Not the anecdote.
- Middle: story, framework, or context that backs it up.
- Final paragraph alone: one question ending with `?`. Nothing after.

**Frontmatter fields (per post):** `status: pending` · `title: <title>` · `group: <name>`.

**Group routing (pick one joined IH group, else `none`):**
- `AI Tools` — AI agents, LLM tooling
- `Artificial Intelligence` — AI strategy, broad AI discussion
- `Building in Public` — build-log, progress updates, honest failures
- `Developers` — technical deep-dives, code snippets, tooling
- `Growth` — distribution, marketing, finding users
- `Ideas and Validation` — user research, feature feedback asks
- `Product Launch` — launch announcements, milestone posts
- `Show IH` — product showcase, "built this" reveals
- `Solo Entrepreneurship` — constraint-driven solo work
- `none` — general feed if no clear match OR group not joined

Group name in `group:` must match EXACTLY (case + spacing). If unsure → `none`.

### 14. `linkedin-carousel.spec.json` + `linkedin-carousel.md` — LinkedIn document post (PDF carousel)

🚨 **Only emit if LinkedIn `weekly.carousels.limit > 0`.** When disabled, skip entirely — `linkedin-post.md` + `linkedin-article.md` are the LinkedIn surface.

🚨 **Emit DATA only. Never HTML/CSS.** The visual is locked in a renderer; you produce structured JSON.

**Two files:**
- `linkedin-carousel.spec.json` — per-slide data. Full shape in `{{pipeline_workspace}}/content-writer/templates/linkedin-carousel-spec.example.json` — copy the shape, replace values with today's topic.
- `linkedin-carousel.md` — title + 150-250-word commentary + hashtags. Voice rules identical to `linkedin-post.md`. Frontmatter: `status: pending`, `title: <100 chars`, `spec_source: <path>`.

**Hard schema constraints (renderer validates and errors on violations):**
- `spec.fields` MUST have exactly 4 entries.
- `spec.fields[].icon` MUST be one of: `target`, `lock`, `notebook`, `alarm`, `lightning`, `shield`, `spark`, `map`. Never invent keys.
- `*_html` fields may contain inline HTML (`<b>`, spans with classes `c1`/`c2`/`c3`/`c4`/`c5` for colored code, `<span class="blank"></span>` for fill-in blanks, entities like `&rarr;` `&mdash;`). Non-`_html` fields are plain text.
- `body_lines` / `template_lines` are string arrays; empty string = blank line.
- Soft caps: headlines ≤60 chars/line, definitions ≤70, takeaways ≤140, support ≤220, descriptions ≤120.

**10-slide order (filled from spec):** cover → hook → code (Mac-window code block of the artifact) → 4 field slides → pattern (side-by-side cards) → CTA (forced-choice question) → bonus (template/checklist).

**When to emit:** themes with a concrete framework, 4-repeatable-field artifact, or structured news peg. SKIP milestones, single-insight quips, unstructured opinion.

**Skip path:** write single-line `linkedin-carousel.md` with `skipped: {reason}`, no spec file. On Tue/Fri a skip fires an Alert at the LinkedIn agent (no fallback post) — only use if reframing genuinely fails.

**Post-emit sanity check:** run `node {{pipeline_workspace}}/image-core/cli.mjs render --platform linkedin --layout carousel --data {spec} --out /tmp/check.pdf`. If non-zero exit, fix spec before continuing.

